    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d758">

                <pb facs="0840" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg728"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 212.11G16/17.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Wilson to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-07-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 19,
                    1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    to-day of the department’s No. 74, of the 12th instant,<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d758-f1"/> inclosing the papers in the extradition case of Heliodoro
                    Garcia, charged with assault with intent to commit murder in the State of
                    California.</p>
                <p>These papers have to-day been presented to the department for foreign affairs,
                    and the extradition of the fugitive has been requested in accordance with treaty
                    stipulations. In case extradition is granted Mr. Cervantes will be promptly
                    advised.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry Lane
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
